<title>ESTONIA: OLAINFARM TO ISSUE NEW SHARES.</title>
<headline>OLAINFARM TO ISSUE NEW SHARES.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Olainfarm, one of the biggest pharmaceutical companies in Latvia, is to issue new shares worth 2.3 million lats, Hansa Investments said on Friday.</p>
<p>The subscription period will be closed on April 17 and the price of a one lat face value share is 2.5 lats.</p>
<p>&quot;It is large placement by Latvian standards,&quot; a Hansa Investments spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>The share placement represents over 30 percent of the new share capital.</p>
<p>The recently-privatised pharmaceutical company is well valued compared Estonia's Tallinna Farmaatsiatehas, whose P/E is three times more expensive, added.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400</p>
